  "interpretation": "The numerical pipeline already supports substantial sentence reconstruction without Sol. The observed extra Sol contribution is four development edits and five fresh-set edits. These small gains, one participant and one session, do not establish robust superiority or a distinctive decoding paradigm.",
  "A_scope": "All structured score families from the actual development call are made available to calibration-only family/ensemble selection. This inherits Sol choice/orchestration of numerical algorithms and selected calibration contexts.",
  "B_scope": "A predetermined inventory is regenerated on fresh neural arrays without reading any Sol-produced helpers, scores, hypotheses, or outputs at application. Calibration contexts are evenly spaced IDs rather than selected by Sol. The algorithm inventory was discovered during development; the workflow still inherits that research discovery.",
  "uncertainty": "Bootstrap ranges resample paired utterances in the same recording block. They are descriptive, do not model within-block correlation, and cannot support participant/session population claims.",
  "comparison_limits": [
    "The deterministic assembly rule estimates unknown word boundaries by uniform or letter-length timing; nonlinear semantic interpretation could exploit the same contexts better. This is one strong auditable comparator, not an optimal algorithmic bound.",
    "Continuous diagnostic printouts (norms/eigenvalues/PC traces) are documented but are not directly word-scored. They contributed to the development algorithm inventory; final-prediction/hypothesis prose is excluded.",
    "The 2340-splice bank contains none of the eight development targets; its exact-match score is not a meaningful standalone compositional benchmark.",
    "The independent trained word-emission baseline was calibrated but not predicted/scored after prioritizing the complete pipeline ablation. It is not used to claim a contribution."
  ],
